  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Countering Transnational Threats on Lake Victoria by Enhancing Border Security Capacities and Coordination between Authorities in Kenya, Uganda and the United Republic of Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to detecting and deterring transnational organized crime (TOC) around the Lake Victoria sub-region, at the crossroads of Kenya, the United Republic of Tanzania and Uganda. It will achieve this principal objective through the following outcomes: i) Kenyan, Tanzanian and Ugandan border authorities on Lake Victoria ports coordinate responses to TOC issues more effectively, ii) improving work environment, tools and knowledge of border management agencies (e.g., Directorate of Citizenship and Immigration Control of Uganda, Immigration Services Department in the United Republic of Tanzania ) to effectively manage ports, iii) enhancing border security around the Lake Victoria through specialized trainings and, iv) improving engagement between the border authorities and maritime border communities around the Lake Victoria sub-region to tackle TOC and trade facilitation related challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
